  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical Assistance for Banking &amp; Financial Services - Guinea</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Banking team advisors are providing intermittent technical assistance to the Central Bank in the following areas: Assisting with the implementation phase of Guineas National Strategy for Financial Inclusion; Providing assistance with the development of a comprehensive e-money issuer (EMI) regulatory framework, including improving the current EMI regulation, developing licensing guidelines, and implementing supervisory policies and procedures; Designing an automated reporting framework for the collection and analysis of data from non-bank financial institutions, including EMIs and microfinance institutions; Assisting the BCRG with the further modernization of the payments system to allow for and interoperability among banks as well as greater participation by non-bank financial institutions;Assisting the BCRG with strengthening supervision of the microfinance sector; and Enabling MSMEs access to credit by: Drafting and adopting new laws for Secured Transactions, Factoring, and Leasing. Designing, Creating, and Launching a Registry of Moveable Assets</narrative>
  </description>
